{"request":{"id":0,"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"initialize","params":{"capabilities":{},"clientInfo":{"name":"opentide-xtask-mcp","version":"1"},"protocolVersion":"2025-06-18"}},"response":{"id":0,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"capabilities":{"prompts":{"listChanged":false},"resources":{"listChanged":false,"subscribe":false},"tools":{"listChanged":false}},"instructions":"opentide: Spec-driven development for agentic detection engineering. opentide gives every detection an ontology and a taxonomy, so it stays threat-aligned, maintainable and fast to ship, with or without agents.\n\nThe catalogue is YAML in the repository: threats (objects/threats/), objectives (objects/objectives/) and rules (objects/rules/). A rule's detection_model is an objective UUID; an objective lists threat UUIDs.\n\nWorkflow:\n1. Search. search (keyword, UUID, technique) and coverage find what exists; get_chaining shows threat -> objective -> rule.\n2. Draft. Start from opentide://templates/{object_type}, check fields against opentide://schemas/{object_type} and opentide://vocabularies/{name}, and write the file with your own tools: this server does not write files.\n3. Validate until clean. Call validation_report with file or uuid after every edit. Each issue has code, severity, message, object_uuid, path, line and column (1-based), help, and fix ({safe, edits}: each edit replaces the text from (line, column) up to (end_line, end_column) with replacement). Apply safe edits as they are: they only respell the same word; check the others against help. explain(code) says what a code means. Repeat until ok is true. While drafting a query, validate_query checks it offline in its platform's language, with no tenant.\n4. Preview. deploy_rule with dry_run true shows the deployment; nothing is sent.\n\nPeople review and merge changes and run real deployments. Call deploy_rule with dry_run false only when a person asks for it. validate_query with live true contacts the tenant with the configured credentials: ask first. run_query with live true runs a read-only query on a tenant and returns its rows: ask first as well.\n\nResults may carry next_actions: [{tool, arguments, command, reason}], the next call to make (command is the same step as an opentide command line). Read the reason before following one.","protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","serverInfo":{"name":"opentide","version":"<VERSION>"}}},"step":"initialize"}
